DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn() function suspends execution of the calling thread un‐
     til the target _t_h_r_e_a_d terminates unless the target _t_h_r_e_a_d has already
     terminated.

     On return from a successful pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn() call with a non-NULL _v_a_l_u_e___p_t_r
     argument, the value passed to pptthhrreeaadd__eexxiitt() by the terminating thread is
     stored in the location referenced by _v_a_l_u_e___p_t_r.  When a pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn()
     returns successfully, the target thread has been terminated.  The results
     of multiple simultaneous calls to pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn() specifying the same tar‐
     get thread are undefined.  If the thread calling pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn() is can‐
     celled, then the target thread is not detached.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ttiimmeeddjjooiinn__nnpp() function is equivalent to the pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn()
     function except it will return ETIMEDOUT if target thread does not exit
     before specified absolute time passes.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ppeeeekkjjooiinn__nnpp() only peeks into the exit status of the speci‐
     fied thread.  If the thread has not exited, the EBUSY error is returned.
     Otherwise, zero is returned and the thread exit value is optionally
     stored into the location of _*_v_a_l_u_e___p_t_r.  The target thread is left un‐
     joined and can be used as an argument for the pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn() family of
     functions again.

     A thread that has exited but remains unjoined counts against
     [_POSIX_THREAD_THREADS_MAX].

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, the described functions return zero.  Otherwise an error
     number is returned to indicate the error or special condition.

EERRRROORRSS
     The pptthhrreeaadd__jjooiinn(), pptthhrreeaadd__ppeeeekkjjooiinn__nnpp(), and pptthhrreeaadd__ttiimmeeddjjooiinn__nnpp()
     functions will fail if:

     [EINVAL]           The implementation has detected that the value speci‐
                        fied by _t_h_r_e_a_d does not refer to a joinable thread.

     [ESRCH]            No thread could be found corresponding to that speci‐
                        fied by the given thread ID, _t_h_r_e_a_d.

     [EDEADLK]          A deadlock was detected or the value of _t_h_r_e_a_d speci‐
                        fies the calling thread.

     [EOPNOTSUPP]       The implementation detected that another caller is al‐
                        ready waiting on _t_h_r_e_a_d.

     Additionally, the pptthhrreeaadd__ttiimmeeddjjooiinn__nnpp() function will fail if:

     [ETIMEDOUT]        The specified absolute time passed while
                        pptthhrreeaadd__ttiimmeeddjjooiinn__nnpp() waited for thread exit.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__ppeeeekkjjooiinn__nnpp() function will also fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The specified thread has not yet exited.

